// Brought to u by MidManStudio
// =============================================================================
// NPM/WASM PUBLISH READINESS  ·  DixScript v1.0.0 (dixscript crate, published)
// =============================================================================
// Everything from the "get npm + wasm ready to publish" pass:
//   1. dixscript path deps in mdix-wasm / mdix-python / mdix-java / mdix-lua
//      now carry version = "1.0.0" too -- a bare path dep can't be
//      cargo-published, crates.io rejects it outright. mdix-cli/mdix-lsp/
//      mdix-ffi already had this right, left untouched here.
//   2. mdix-wasm: MdixDatabase.validateSchema wired up for real -- it was
//      documented at the top of schema.rs but never attached to the
//      #[wasm_bindgen] impl block, so it was unreachable from JS entirely.
//      Same shape of miss as the mergeWith regression (already fixed,
//      already tested) -- this is that same wiring for schema.rs.
//   3. mdix-wasm/tests/web.rs -- 4 new regression tests for validateSchema
//      (passes on matching data, reports a missing field, reports a wrong
//      type, confirms one MdixSchema instance validates multiple databases)
//   4. mdix-npm: index.ts now re-exports the FULL mdix-wasm surface --
//      DLM compile/decompile, merge, schema validation, watch. Previously
//      only MdixDatabase/MdixBuilder were exported: 11 of 13 lib.rs
//      bindings were invisible from npm despite being fully implemented
//      in the compiled wasm binary either way.
//   5. mdix-npm/src/types.ts -- added MdixMergeStrategy, MdixArrayMergeStrategy,
//      MdixMergeConflict, MdixValidationError(Kind) so the JSON-shaped
//      conflicts()/errors() returns aren't just `any`.
//   6. mdix-npm/tests/dlm-merge-schema-watch.test.mjs -- new file, 16 tests
//      covering all four newly-exposed features end to end (node:test,
//      same convention as the existing enum-mixed-data test).
//   7. mdix-npm/README.md -- documents Merging / Schema validation /
//      Hot reload / DLM, each with a working example. Docs link kept to
//      the one verified URL, https://dixscript-docs.pages.dev.
//   8. .github/workflows/wasm-npm-publish.yml -- updated the header
//      comment that flagged this exact export gap; it's closed now, so
//      the "flagged, not fixed" wording would've been stale otherwise.
//
// NOT included here on purpose:
//   - rust-version bump. All 7 dixscript-dependent crates still claim
//     rust-version = "1.70", but dixscript itself declares "1.85" -- that's
//     a real mismatch (false MSRV metadata), flagged, wanted a go-ahead
//     before touching it across seven files.
//
// Every replacement file below is a NESTED archive entry, so each one
// resolves straight to target_root + its own path -- no overrides:: block
// needed, nothing here is ambiguous even with 4 separate Cargo.toml's
// bundled in the same archive (that's the whole point of nesting them --
// see MDIX_SCAFFOLD_SKILL.md, "Replacements Templates").
// =============================================================================

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "MidManStudio"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@DATA(
  description = "cargo.toml versioned-dixscript fix + wasm validateSchema bugfix + full npm re-export/types/tests/README for npm+wasm publish readiness"
  target_root = "."
)
